      "headline": "Bolsonaro awaits STF authorization for shoulder surgery while STM weighs potential loss of military rank",
      "summary": "Former president Jair Bolsonaro, under house arrest since March, sought court approval to leave confinement for surgery on a torn rotator cuff; the Solicitor General (PGR) endorsed the request and it awaits STF Justice Alexandre de Moraes' decision. Separately, the Superior Military Tribunal (STM) authorized collection of military service documents to evaluate whether Bolsonaro should lose his captain's reserve rank following his STF conviction in the coup-plot case. Justice Cármen Lúcia also rejected a habeas corpus petition aimed at modifying his house arrest conditions."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Senate CCJ to hold confirmation hearing for Lula's STF nominee Jorge Messias on April 29",
      "summary": "The Senate's Constitution and Justice Committee is scheduled to hear Jorge Messias, Brazil's current Solicitor General and Lula's nominee to the STF, on April 29 — more than five months after his nomination. Messias has been lobbying senators for votes and is expected to be confirmed, with the Lula government's liaison minister Zé Guimarães saying negotiations are on track for approval."
    }
  ]
